x11-web-wayland-server — provenance and licensing
=================================================

This crate is a derivative work of **waylandcraft**.

    Upstream project : waylandcraft
    Upstream URL     : https://github.com/EVV1E/waylandcraft
    Upstream commit  : 233d1431e6acbad1d0c47dfba44d971ce0cebfe8
    Upstream license : GNU General Public License, version 3 (GPLv3)

waylandcraft is a smithay-based Wayland compositor that renders client
surfaces into Minecraft. The Minecraft/JNI half is not used here; what
was taken is the compositor half — the smithay state wiring, xdg-shell
handling, wl_shm buffer attach, and the hand-rolled wl_seat with its
xkbcommon keymap.

Because waylandcraft is GPLv3, every file in this crate that is derived
from it carries a header comment naming the upstream file, the commit
above, and the license, and all such derived *source* is confined to
this crate. No waylandcraft-derived source exists anywhere else in the
x11-web repository.

Scope of the copyleft (read this part)
--------------------------------------

Source containment is not obligation containment. Any binary that links
this crate is a combined work with the GPLv3 code in it and can only be
conveyed under GPLv3. Today that is exactly one binary:

    crates/sidecar-wayland  ->  x11-web-sidecar-wayland
                                (built into Dockerfile.sidecar-wayland)

Both that crate's Cargo.toml and this one declare
`license = "GPL-3.0-only"`, and the runtime stage of
Dockerfile.sidecar-wayland ships ./COPYING beside the binary, because
GPLv3 sections 4 and 5 require the License to travel with the work.

Crates outside that link graph are unaffected — x11-web-backend,
x11-web-x11-server, x11-web-sidecar, x11-web-wire and the frontend
neither contain nor link any waylandcraft-derived code. (The two
non-dependent Dockerfiles stub these two crates out of the workspace
precisely so nothing links them by accident.)

Files derived from upstream
---------------------------

    src/utils.rs      <- native/src/utils.rs
                         Serial/timestamp helpers, ported verbatim.

    src/output.rs     <- native/src/output.rs
                         Hand-rolled wl_output v4 global. The unused
                         `bounds` concept was dropped; resize() is
                         driven by WindowRouter::set_screen_size
                         instead of the Android surface size.

    src/state.rs      <- native/src/lib.rs
                         Compositor state struct + smithay delegate
                         wiring. The EGL/dmabuf, xwayland-satellite,
                         .desktop-launcher and wl_data_device fields
                         and their handlers were deleted; commit()
                         gained the shm readback; the JNI request
                         queues were replaced by direct handling.

    src/surface.rs    <- native/src/bridge.rs
                         Buffer attach (shm + single-pixel), surface
                         tree walk, viewport/damage handling, frame
                         callback drain. Every JNI-ism (handle tables,
                         jptr marshalling, bind_java_type!) removed;
                         the dmabuf attach arm deleted and the
                         resulting reachable `unreachable!()` turned
                         into a logged error.

    src/seat.rs       <- native/src/seat.rs
                         wl_seat / wl_pointer / wl_keyboard globals
                         and the xkb keymap SealedFile. The trailing
                         relative-pointer, pointer-constraints and
                         cursor-shape sections were dropped (out of
                         scope, and they carry the only let-chains,
                         which would force edition 2024).

Files written from scratch (not derived)
----------------------------------------

    src/lib.rs, src/server.rs, src/router.rs, src/windows.rs,
    src/input.rs, src/pixels.rs, src/translate.rs, src/decoration.rs,
    examples/headless.rs, test-tools/wl-input-probe.c

test-tools/wl-input-probe.c is a plain libwayland-client program (no
smithay, no waylandcraft code) written for this repository's e2e
suite. It is compiled into the sidecar image by
Dockerfile.sidecar-wayland, not by cargo.

